# Repo-wide secrets loaded by stacks that opt in. bootstrap.ps1 copies this
# tracked placeholder to the gitignored .env; replace it before starting.
#
# AgentMemory is an unattended API client and needs ONE chat-completions
# credential. It reads that credential as OPENAI_API_KEY whichever provider is
# serving, because it speaks the OpenAI wire protocol either way. This file loads
# AFTER agentmemory/.env, so this is the only place the credential can win --
# setting it in the stack .env has no effect.
#
# --- provider A: vLLM on lambda-dual (the current deployment) ----------------
# Set OPENAI_API_KEY to the same value as VLLM_API_KEY below, and set the
# endpoint and model in agentmemory/.env. Nothing is billed. Note the 16,384
# token context: agentmemory/README.md, "vLLM on lambda-dual" covers the prompt
# bounds that depends on, and the reasoning_effort trap.
#
# --- provider B: OpenAI API -------------------------------------------------
# Set OPENAI_API_KEY to an sk-proj-... key with API billing enabled; a Codex
# OAuth login is not a reusable container secret. Create it INSIDE the dedicated
# billing project (agentmemory/README.md, "Authoritative cost reconciliation") --
# a key from outside that project works fine for inference but its usage never
# appears in project-scoped cost sync, which reads as $0.00 rather than as an
# error. Restrict it to Chat completions -> Request. Rotating it:
# agentmemory/README.md, "Rotating either key".
OPENAI_API_KEY=replace-me-with-the-active-provider-key

# vLLM on lambda-dual, reached over TAILSCALE. VLLM_API_KEY is the credential to
# mirror into OPENAI_API_KEY above; the rest is the canonical record of the
# endpoint and is also read by other host tooling.
#
# Use the TAILNET IPv4 (100.x.y.z), not a LAN address and not the MagicDNS name:
#   - A LAN address (the old 10.30.1.20) only works from that physical network.
#     A laptop on any other network cannot reach it at all.
#   - MagicDNS resolves on the HOST via Tailscale's resolver at 100.100.100.100.
#     AgentMemory dials from INSIDE a container, whose DNS is Docker's embedded
#     resolver. That happens to forward the tailnet name on Docker Desktop for
#     Mac today (measured: it does), but it is not a documented guarantee and it
#     differs by platform and version. The 100.x address depends on none of it.
# Find it with:  tailscale ip -4 lambda-dual      (or: tailscale status)
#
# HOST reachability is not sufficient evidence -- a container's egress is a
# separate path. Verify from a container before trusting this:
#   docker run --rm curlimages/curl:8.14.1 -sS -o /dev/null \
#     -w '%{http_code}\n' --max-time 8 http://100.x.y.z:8000/v1/models
# 401 means reachable (up, needs the key). 000 means no route -- see
# docs/new-machine-macos.md for the host-forwarder fallback.
#
# VLLM_MAX_TOKENS is the model's CONTEXT length, not an output cap. Do not copy
# it into AgentMemory's MAX_TOKENS -- that would request the whole context as
# completion tokens and leave no room for the prompt.
VLLM_API_KEY=replace-me-with-vllm-key
VLLM_BASE_URL=http://100.x.y.z:8000/v1
VLLM_MAX_TOKENS=16384
VLLM_DEFAULT_MODEL=qwen3-8b-awq
